{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/843073-new-mechanics-for-the-shartha","id":843073,"title":"New Mechanics for the Shartha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-06T11:48:53-08:00","id":843073,"title":"New Mechanics for the Shartha","content":"So, this is a little something I cobbled together from the new 2E paradigm on the Hosts, the Predators book, and Cinder's fabulous homebrew <i>shartha</i>. Criticism and suggestions on how to improve it would be greatly appreciated, and if anyone actually uses it in play, let me know how it went. I'm still trying to think up appropriate mechanics for Conditions for Hosts inhabiting a human body.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <b>Systems for the <i>Shartha</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Base Traits</i><ul><li>All Host Shards begin at Size 1<ul><li>They start with Rank 1<ul><li>Possess Dread Powers equivalent to average Numina for Rank<ul><li>All Hosts gain the Discorporation Dread Power when possessing a body.</li> <li>Azlu begin with Gauntlet Webs and Wall Climb for free</li> <li>Beshilu begin with Gnaw Gauntlet and Warp Shard for free</li> <li>Razilu begin with Cold Blood and Ouroboros for free</li> </ul></li> <li>Generally possess Merit dots equal to the number of Dread Powers they possess.</li> </ul></li> <li>Hosts not possessing a body use the three simplified Attributes to start<ul><li><b>Beshilu and Azlu:</b> Power 1, Finesse 3, Resistance 1<ul><li>Speed Species Factor: +10</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Razilu: </b>Power 1, Finesse 2, Resistance 2<ul><li>Speed Species Factor: +8</li> </ul></li> <li>They use the <i>higher</i> of Finesse or Power to calculate Defense in this shape.</li> <li>Apply Rank as Skills when not possessing a human.</li> </ul></li> <li>Hosts possess a pool of Essence equal to Resistance. This expands to Resolve + Composure + Rank once they become a Hybrid.<ul><li>They regain Essence by eating the animals they represent, attacking Werewolves and Spirits, or (once they become Hybrids) by eating humans.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>All Hosts may Reach across the Gauntlet and project their senses into the <i>Hisil</i> like Werewolves can.</li> <li>A Host possessing a human gains an appropriate Condition<ul><li>Heart Eater (Beshilu), Hollow Rider (Azlu), Visceral Nest (Razilu)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <i>Power Increase</i><ul><li>Should the Host devour another Shard of the appropriate type, consume a dead werewolf, or take over a human, they may gain up to their Rank in Attributes or Dread Powers<ul><li>When possessing a human, the Host uses their Simplified Attributes as their Mental and Social Attributes, and take on the host body\u2019s Physical Attributes. Once every three days, one of the host body\u2019s Physical Attributes deteriorates.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Joining:</b> When the Host gathers enough power to be able to hold 5 Essence at once, they may become a full Hybrid, which is treated as though they are a Spirit using the Claim Manifestation effect. Just like the Claimed, a Shartha Hybrid doesn\u2019t have any Attribute or Dread Power limits, but once they\u2019ve been killed and Discorporated, they are once again subject to the limits of Rank.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Dread Powers</b><br /> <br /> <i>General</i><br /> <br /> <b>Coward\u2019s Edge:</b> The <i>shartha</i> is unfailingly capable of sensing Uratha up to their (Rank x 100) yards away. Different Hosts feel this as a different sensation, Azlu may feel their stomach cramp up and Beshilu may feel shivers running up their spine.<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Size: </b>The <i>shartha</i> is massive, taking on some of its Pangaean progenitor\u2019s godlike size and might. They gain their Rank in Size, Armour equal to their dots of Resistance, and gain the 8-again quality when attacking creatures or objects of smaller Size than they are. They also take on the appearance of a massive occurrence of the animal they are based off of.<br /> <br /> <b>Preserve the Hollow Shell: </b>A human host body taken by the Host multiplies the period it takes for Physical Attributes to decay by the Host\u2019s Rank. Ergo, a Rank 5 <i>Shartha</i> loses a dot of a Physical Attribute once every 15 days.<br /> <br /> <b>Writhing Nest: </b>The horrible, twisted Essence of the Shard\u2019s divine soul courses through the veins of the human host, filling their body with a coursing horde of vermin. Whenever the Host suffers Lethal damage, instead of bleeding a number of these pests rush out. This functions like the moderate Poisoned Tilt. For a point of Essence, it may be boosted to the grave Poisoned Tilt for the scene. As a drawback, this also triples the rate of the body\u2019s decay. Every hour, about (10 x Rank) instances of the creatures are produced. Some exceptionally potent <i>shartha</i> will \u2018bleed off\u2019 these creatures- either just to reduce the pressure on their body, or as a quick Essence snack.<br /> <br /> <i>Azlu</i><br /> <b>Egg Sac (Requires Rank 5): </b>A rare and treasured Dread Power among the <i>Azlu</i>, the dread creature that possesses this ability is the most rare of the Spinner Hag\u2019s daughters- an <i>Azlu</i> Crone. Their abdomen swells into a fleshy orb, perhaps even resembling a true spider\u2019s abdomen, and may lay pearl-sized eggs through a fleshy sphincter. For a point of Essence, they may lay up to (Rank x Resistance or Stamina) eggs. For 10 points of Essence, they lay a single egg that hatches into a new Shard.<br /> <br /> <b>Unearthly Allure: </b>The potent soul of the Shard can overwhelm any sense that something is wrong with their host body. They permanently gain a +3 bonus to Social actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural Anatomy:</b> The <i>Azlu\u2019s</i> host body warps and mutates into a form more befitting of an heir to the Spinner Hag. They gain a number of features from the list below equal to their Rank. This Dread Power can be taken multiple times, but bear in mind that no Azlu may possess more than twelve limbs.<ul><li><b>Additional Arms:</b> The <i>Azlu</i> gains a +1 bonus to Strength for lifting, carrying, grappling, or inflicting Brawl damage.</li> <li><b>Additional Legs:</b> The <i>Azlu</i> gains a +1 bonus to Strength for Speed and balance</li> <li><b>Additional Eyes: </b>The <i>Azlu</i> gains a +1 bonus to Perception checks</li> </ul><br /> <i>Beshilu</i><br /> <br /> <b>Glowing Eyes: </b>The lurid golden glow that signals out the Rat Host are enough to impair their foes. The Storyteller may judge that this light is enough to allow their opponents to see, but within close combat quarters, should the <i>Beshilu</i> make eye contact with their opponent it imposes the Blinded Tilt to both eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Hive Call: </b>Taking up some of their progenitor\u2019s psychic might, the <i>Beshilu</i> may spend a point of Essence and roll Wits + Empathy in order to send a short message to every Rat Host within their permanent Essence score in miles. They may send a sentence per success. Werewolves with Harmony of 6-4 hear the use of this Dread Power as a painful \u2018shrieking\u2019 in their mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Poison Tumors: </b>The <i>Beshilu</i> grows skin cancers that hang off their body in black and purple growths. These tumors emit a horrific scent within several yards of the Rat Host, forcing anyone who comes within (Rank x Stamina) of the <i>Beshilu</i> to roll Resolve + Composure to stand the smell <i>or</i> may choose to hold their breath. Add +2 to all attempts to track the Rat Host by scent. Those who come within their radius suffer the moderate Sick Tilt, and should the Beshilu touch someone and spend a point of Essence they suffer the grave Sick Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Prophet\u2019s Vision (Rank 5 Required): </b>A rare and treasured Dread Power among the <i>Beshilu</i>, the typically craven Rat Host will fight to the death to protect these horrific creatures. A true heir to the Plague King\u2019s power, they permanently suffer the Blinded Tilt to both eyes, but may use the Glory Facet of the Insight Gift (Reading the World\u2019s Loom) at no Essence cost, substituting Rank for Glory. Additionally, should the Host die, they may reflexively spend a point of Essence to summon a swarm of rats, even if they don\u2019t possess the Beastmaster Dread Power, with the command to eat their body. If a single rat manages to devour 10 Essence, they warp into a new Beshilu Shard.<br /> <br /> <b>Scentless: </b>Rat Hosts with this Dread Power become exceptionally difficult to track by smell, as their scent is reduced to an infinitesimal glimmer on the senses. All attempts to track the <i>Beshilu</i> by scent suffer their Rank as a penalty.<br /> <br /> <i>Razilu</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cold Blood (Innate): </b>The <i>Razilu\u2019s</i> reptilian metabolism allows her to add +3 to her Stamina for resisting hunger, thirst, poison, heat, or lack of air. Once per scene, they can spend a point of Essence to strike with incredible speed, gaining the highest Initiative for one turn, regardless of her roll. If two Snake Hosts use this power in the same turn, use their normal Initiative value to determine who goes first.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Grip: </b>Channeling the might of the largest of constrictor snakes, the <i>Razilu</i> is capable of leveraging immense force when grappling with their foes. By spending a point of Essence, the Razilu doubles their Strength for a turn while Grappling.<br /> <br /> <b>Hydra (Requires Rank 5): </b>Only the oldest and mightiest of the <i>Razilu</i> possess this extremely rare and powerful Dread Power. Considering the <i>Razilu</i> are also extremely rare and powerful, this should say something. Their brethren bow to the might of these serpentine abominations. Each attack that inflicts one or more points of Lethal damage causes a new head to sprout on a sinuous neck within seconds, but Bashing or Aggravated damage doesn\u2019t trigger this effect. Each head adds +1 to the <i>Razilu\u2019s</i> Health, but as their wounds heal they shed heads in excess of their permanent Essence rating. With multiple heads, they are capable of making a Brawl attack using Autofire rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Ouroboros (Innate): </b>A predator among predators, the Snake Host is a creature that can send even the mightiest of <i>Beshilu</i> and <i>Azlu</i> fleeing in abject terror. Unlike other Hosts, stuck devouring one another or eating their way through humans and werewolves, the <i>Razilu</i> are capable of devouring Shards of other Hosts for their power. When a <i>shartha</i> dies near the <i>Razilu</i>, they may spend a point of Essence and roll Resolve + Intimidation + Rank vs. the target\u2019s Resolve + Composure + Rank. Should the Snake Host succeed, their target will not discorporate for a number of minutes equal to their successes. All the other Host can do is watch and wait as the <i>Razilu</i> hunkers down to eat.<br /> <br /> <b>Swallow: </b>Like all serpents, the <i>Razilu</i> is capable of swallowing things much too large to fit through their jaws. The Host with this Dread Power is capable of horrific acts of consumption and regurgitation. The <i>Razilu</i> spends a point of Essence and rolls Stamina + Survival with a Target Number equal to the Size of the object, with an interval of a minute between each roll. They may only hold a total Size of objects up to their own Size. They begin to gnaw on the object, which causes their jaws to distort and dislocate obscenely- long planes fold as though made of clay to fit down the Snake Host\u2019s throat. This mulch is not digested unless they choose to digest it. They cannot consume living things, but a dead body is fair game.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural Anatomy:</b> The <i>Razilu\u2019s</i> body warps into a shape more fitting for a child of the Sea Serpent. They gain a number of features from the list below equal to their Rank. This Dread Power may be taken multiple times, but bear in mind that they may not possess more than twelve limbs. If they take the Tail modification more than once, they lose all of their legs.<ul><li><b>Additional Arms:</b> The <i>Razilu</i> gains a +1 bonus to Strength for lifting, carrying, grappling, or inflicting Brawl damage.</li> <li><b>Additional Legs:</b> The <i>Razilu</i> gains a +1 bonus to Strength for Speed and balance</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Hood: </b>The <i>Razilu</i> gains a +1 bonus to all Intimidation rolls. Taking this modification multiple times doesn\u2019t produce multiple cobra-like hoods, but makes the original one larger and more impressive.</li> <li><b>Forked Tongue: </b>The <i>Razilu</i> gains a +1 bonus to all Perception rolls to sense or track enemies.</li> <li><b>Tail: </b>The <i>Razilu</i> grows a thick, fleshy tail. This grants a +1 bonus to Strength for the purposes of Speed and Grappling. If this modification is taken multiple times, every time past the first adds +1 Size to the Snake Host as their lower body turns into a massive serpentine tail. Other bonuses scale as appropriate.<ul><li><b>Rattle (Tail Required): </b>The <i>Razilu</i> grows a hollow chain of scales like a rattlesnake, which grants them the 8-again quality to Intimidation rolls.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T18:17:57-08:00","id":843721,"title":"","content":"I really like this, i've been working on my own more in depth shartha stuff on and off and am happy to see that others are thinking along the same lines.<br /> <br /> I propose that each Shartha should have two anchors, the first anchor would be the <i>Imperative; </i>the imperative is the instinctual motivation imprinted on each of the shartha by their monstrous progenitors. each brood of shartha would share the same imperative. for example the Beshilu would all share the imperative to weaken through the gauntlet, regaining a point of willpower as they do so and regaining all will power when they take great personal risks to bring the two worlds together or when they reduce the gauntlet rating to 0. the second anchor would be its eccentricity (working title im not sold on it yet) the eccentricity is that individual shartha's deviation of personalty away from the horrific spirit-god that first spawned it. a shartha's eccentricity rewards it for reinforcing its sense of individualism that separate it from the others of its kind.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of replacing rank with a supernatural advantage as the shartha are distinctly outside of the Darwinian hierarchy of the shadow courts. I'd rip the name of synthesis strait form the predators supplement as the name just fits far to perfectly, in this case synthesis represents how close the shartha is to reconstituting the original monstrosity that created it. id then model increasing synthesis after how vampires increases their blood potency through diablerie in 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T05:51:36-08:00","id":843912,"title":"","content":"2E doesn't really like using Power/Finesse/Resistance for non-ephemerals.It's sort of become a literal consequence of their mind body and soul all being the same thing rather than an actual rules simplification.<br /> <br /> If they do want actual simplified traits, they use a different system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T16:51:13-08:00","id":844207,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I haven't <i>quite </i>grokked the Horror Creation rules just yet and I wrote this with the paradigm that Hosts, as half-spirit things, are more like Claimed when they've become a Hybrid than anything else. Because of that, I figured a system that didn't <i>really </i>stack on the Attributes would be appropriate, and I used the Claimed as a guide. Obviously it isn't perfect, but I'm reasonably happy with how the <i>shartha</i> increase in power.<br /> <br /> That being said, this was written with the intention of Hosts as antagonists-only, seeing as Dread Powers aren't exactly PC material in the same way Numina or Influences aren't usually PC material. Didn't really see the need to give them specialized anchors, or a Power Stat like the Major Templates do, but your suggestions do sound pretty good for more PC material <i>shartha </i>WelshBoi. Not entirely sure <i>I'd</i> want to play one, but it's an interesting idea and could work quite well for a PvP game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T03:27:01-08:00","id":844415,"title":"","content":"I defiantly agree with the Shartha being antagonists abd not really pc material but I don't see why that shouldn't mean they shouldn't get anchors. Ghosts, Angels hell even the stric pick one vice as a rough guide to thier inhuman motivations why not the Shartha. I'm a big believer that if I'm going to use an antagonist for any longer that one or two sessions then it better have a personality and motivations just as fully fleshed out as the player characters or there is no reward for them engaging it on anything other than a physical level. I think anchors are a good tool for helping to define that antagonist/npc's drives and personality with in the context of its stats.<br /> Also agreeing with the point that they shouldnt use simplified stats. The horror of the Shartha is that they are a different type of dark reflection of the forsaken than the pure, that they are abominations of twisted spirit-flesh created by a primordial spiritual entity. And I think that needs to be sold mechanically as well as narratively","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}